Report: Exact construction, state access and native output for all four PCG generator types
21 claims; 0 removal(s).
  run_ids: null -> ["702c172f-820b-47b7-9b00-ecff7d926779"]
  crate: null -> "rand_pcg"
  version: null -> "0.10.2"
  title: null -> "Exact construction, state access and native output for all four PCG generator types"
  explanation: null -> "For rand_pcg 0.10.2, state returns the exact stored word for Lcg64Xsh32, Lcg128Xsl64, Lcg128CmDxsm64 and Mcg128Xsl64. For the three LCG types, stream returns the stored increment shifted logically right by one; from_state preserves the given state and stores increment=(stream<<1) OR 1, discarding the highest stream bit. Their new constructors normalize that increment and initialize state=((input_state+increment)*multiplier+increment), with state-width modular arithmetic. The multipliers are 6364136223846793005, 47026247687942121848144207491837523525, and 15750249268501108917, respectively. Mcg128Xsl64::new stores input_state OR 1. Each of these fourteen original APIs terminates normally in the model for arbitrary scalar inputs. The prior Lcg64Xsh32::try_next_u32 exact PCG-XSH-RR output/state theorem is also retained, for fifteen initial proved API bodies. Six further body proofs establish try_next_u64 and try_next_u32 for Lcg128Xsl64, Mcg128Xsl64 and Lcg128CmDxsm64, for twenty-one API bodies total. The XSL-RR variants permute the newly advanced state; the CM-DXSM variant permutes the old state and then advances. Their 32-bit methods return the low 32 bits of the corresponding 64-bit result with exactly the same state update. The original standard Result::map body and the original conversion closures are included in the proof. Selected official translations are byte-identical under default and serde configurations; serde trait implementations remain unproved."
  trusted_assumptions: null -> "The Rust compiler, official Charon/Aeneas translation, official Aeneas scalar models and Lean kernel are trusted. No custom external models, source adaptations or local trusted helper contracts are used. All twenty-one API theorem dependency audits permit only propext, Classical.choice and Quot.sound. Wrapping arithmetic, shifts, casts and rotations use official standard-library models, rather than proofs of Rust std implementation bodies. The original Result::map body is extracted and proved through its actual closure calls, rather than supplied by a custom model."
  tool_version_id: null -> "aeneas-be86ab0f1989d04944292b345b24c435be3ad10a"
  environment: null -> "Unchanged crates.io rand_pcg 0.10.2 Rust sources and Cargo.toml; original archive/hash checks, tests and regeneration comparisons retained in evidence. Rust nightly-2026-09-17; Charon 08d7c9d50144bd84848212c24701253585e90d1f; official Aeneas frontend/library be86ab0f1989d04944292b345b24c435be3ad10a; Lean 4.35.0. Official targeted extraction includes each actual original body, macro-expanded state helpers and private constructor helpers. Separate all-features (serde) extraction is retained in evidence/serde; generated Lean is byte-identical to the default extraction. Six additional output bodies and core::result::Result::map are included via the official --include core::result selection. Two output-permutation helper theorems are audited separately."
  evidence_url: null -> "https://github.com/nyuichi/rust-crate-proofs/tree/57c4d16e1184f84353db90589bc3cb601f89cb85"
  limitations: null -> "Coverage is limited to the twenty-one named bodies, default or serde features, x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu. Model states need not have odd increments: the getter theorem reports the logical shift for every modeled state, but no save/restore identity is claimed for an arbitrary even-increment state. from_state/new normalize the increment exactly as specified. Advance, seed bytes/from_seed/seed_from_u64, Lcg64Xsh32::try_next_u64, byte-buffer filling, RNG callbacks/forking, manual Debug, serde and inherited/default/external blanket APIs remain unproved. The proof does not establish period, statistical quality or cryptographic security. Other targets and dependency feature combinations were not checked."
