  "environment": "Unchanged crates.io rand_pcg 0.10.2 Rust sources and Cargo.toml; original archive/hash checks, tests and regeneration comparisons retained in evidence. Rust nightly-2026-09-17; Charon 08d7c9d50144bd84848212c24701253585e90d1f; official Aeneas frontend/library be86ab0f1989d04944292b345b24c435be3ad10a; Lean 4.35.0. Official targeted extraction includes each actual original body, macro-expanded state helpers and private constructor helpers. Separate all-features (serde) extraction is retained in evidence/serde; generated Lean is byte-identical to the default extraction. Six additional output bodies and core::result::Result::map are included via the official --include core::result selection. Two output-permutation helper theorems are audited separately.",
  "evidence_url": "https://github.com/nyuichi/rust-crate-proofs/tree/57c4d16e1184f84353db90589bc3cb601f89cb85",
  "explanation": "For rand_pcg 0.10.2, state returns the exact stored word for Lcg64Xsh32, Lcg128Xsl64, Lcg128CmDxsm64 and Mcg128Xsl64. For the three LCG types, stream returns the stored increment shifted logically right by one; from_state preserves the given state and stores increment=(stream<<1) OR 1, discarding the highest stream bit. Their new constructors normalize that increment and initialize state=((input_state+increment)*multiplier+increment), with state-width modular arithmetic. The multipliers are 6364136223846793005, 47026247687942121848144207491837523525, and 15750249268501108917, respectively. Mcg128Xsl64::new stores input_state OR 1. Each of these fourteen original APIs terminates normally in the model for arbitrary scalar inputs. The prior Lcg64Xsh32::try_next_u32 exact PCG-XSH-RR output/state theorem is also retained, for fifteen initial proved API bodies. Six further body proofs establish try_next_u64 and try_next_u32 for Lcg128Xsl64, Mcg128Xsl64 and Lcg128CmDxsm64, for twenty-one API bodies total. The XSL-RR variants permute the newly advanced state; the CM-DXSM variant permutes the old state and then advances. Their 32-bit methods return the low 32 bits of the corresponding 64-bit result with exactly the same state update. The original standard Result::map body and the original conversion closures are included in the proof. Selected official translations are byte-identical under default and serde configurations; serde trait implementations remain unproved.",
  "limitations": "Coverage is limited to the twenty-one named bodies, default or serde features, x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu. Model states need not have odd increments: the getter theorem reports the logical shift for every modeled state, but no save/restore identity is claimed for an arbitrary even-increment state. from_state/new normalize the increment exactly as specified. Advance, seed bytes/from_seed/seed_from_u64, Lcg64Xsh32::try_next_u64, byte-buffer filling, RNG callbacks/forking, manual Debug, serde and inherited/default/external blanket APIs remain unproved. The proof does not establish period, statistical quality or cryptographic security. Other targets and dependency feature combinations were not checked.",
